# Which country has the most women in parliament?
subtitle: "Two clues, four flags: find the country whose parliament is nearly two-thirds women, then learn how it got there and what seats can't tell you."
tags: ["geography","history","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Not the one you think\" note \"Most women in parliament\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Leda | a youthful, bright quiz host; curious, not overexcited","b":"gemini:Puck | a curious co-host guessing out loud; relaxed and good-humoured, never exaggerated","take":"lines"}

## Which country has the most women in parliament?
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Five countries had more women than men in parliament in 2025
      authors: Hannah Ritchie and Pablo Arriagada, Our World in Data, from V-Dem
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/data-insights/five-countries-had-more-women-than-men-in-parliament-in-2025
      finding: 'share of seats held by women in 2025: Rwanda about 63.8 %, Cuba 55.7 %, Nicaragua 55.0 %, Bolivia 50.8 %, Mexico 50.2 %'
    - id: share
      title: Share of women in parliament
      authors: Our World in Data, from V-Dem
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-of-women-in-parliament
      finding: world average 27 % in 2025; Sweden 45 %, Iceland 46 %
    - id: herre
      title: Women have made major advances in politics within the last century, but progress has been mixed
      authors: Bastian Herre, Our World in Data
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/women-political-advances
      finding: in 2008, the Rwandan parliament became the first to have more than 50 % women
    - id: regime
      title: Political regime (Regimes of the World)
      authors: Our World in Data, from V-Dem
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/political-regime
      finding: in 2025 Rwanda and Nicaragua are electoral autocracies, Cuba a closed autocracy
    - id: unwomen
      title: Revisiting Rwanda five years after record-breaking parliamentary elections
      authors: UN Women
      year: 2018
      url: https://www.unwomen.org/en/news/stories/2018/8/feature-rwanda-women-in-parliament
      finding: Rwanda's 2003 constitution reserves 30 % of seats in decision-making bodies for women (24 of 80 in the lower house)

